{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The free wait was served in full. The trip was scheduled for 07:45 and the driver reached the pickup at 07:39:30, so under POL-NS-21 the wait runs from the scheduled time (07:45) and expires at 07:50; the driver cancelled at 07:51:40, and the trip record's own derived free_wait block returns cancelled_after_free_wait = true with 400 s from the wait's start to the cancellation. The driver in fact waited past even the platform's own short timer, which expired at 07:44:35.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05058", "EV-GPS-05058"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-21"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.free_wait.cancelled_after_free_wait",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The arrival event is corroborated by the GPS trace, as POL-NS-21's arrival test requires. The nearest fix to the pickup point sits 1.76 m away at 07:40:40 with a reported accuracy of 3 m, well inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius, and the trace's derived arrival_check returns corroborated = true with accuracy_reported = true. The trace itself is clean: 47 fixes at 30 s intervals from 07:28:40 to 07:51:40, 100% coverage, no gaps and a maximum gap of 30 s, far under the 120 s policy impairment threshold.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-05058", "EV-TRIP-05058"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-21"],
      "relies_on": "gps_trace.derived.v7.arrival_check",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's contact obligation under POL-NS-23 is satisfied on its own terms, so the fee is not voided on that ground. The record shows two in-app chat messages sent by the driver (07:40:00, read 07:40:22; 07:46:20, read 07:46:30) and two in-app calls placed by the driver (07:47:30, unanswered, rang 28 s; 07:50:10, unanswered, rang 20 s) — every one of them before the 07:51:40 cancellation. The derived contact_before_cancel block returns obligation_met = true with call_count 2 and message_count 2.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-05058", "EV-TRIP-05058"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-23"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.contact_before_cancel.obligation_met",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider has no counter-ground under POL-NS-24. The driver-no-show deadline is scheduled 07:45 plus 5 minutes, i.e. 07:50, and the driver was at the pickup from 07:39:30, so arrived_by_deadline is true; there is neither a full refund on that clause nor the 5.00 SGD goodwill credit, which requires both a late arrival and a failure to attempt contact — and contact was attempted twice.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05058", "EV-GPS-05058", "EV-CHAT-05058"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-24"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.driver_deadline.arrived_by_deadline",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "With the wait, the arrival and the contact obligation all met, the conditions of POL-NS-22 are made out and the 5.00 SGD fee belongs to the driver as compensation for time and fuel. The amount charged is exactly the policy fee — fee_charged_sgd 5.00 against policy_fee_sgd 5.00, fee_matches_policy = true — so no fee-amount referral arises either, and POL-NS-22 directs DRIVER_COMPENSATION with amount_sgd and driver_compensation_sgd both equal to the fee charged, 5.00 SGD each.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-05058", "EV-TRIP-05058"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-22"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.derived.money.fee_charged_sgd",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The 07:59:40 ledger entry is an interim reversal 'pending review', not a determination of this dispute: the ledger still reads payment_status REFUNDED with refund_issued_sgd 5.00, and the 5.00 SGD was withheld from the driver. That is why the party-relative reading of POL-GEN-03 matters — NO_ACTION means the present state stands, and here the present state leaves the refunded 5.00 with the rider and nothing with the driver. Reading the outcome off the record, the driver's claim is vindicated only by DRIVER_COMPENSATION of 5.00 SGD.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-05058", "EV-TRIP-05058"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.refund_issued_sgd",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's answer — that the driver arrived early and therefore the cancellation was not her fault — is no answer under the policy. POL-NS-21 anchors the free wait to scheduled_at precisely in the case where the driver arrives before the scheduled time, so an early arrival neither shortens the wait the driver owes nor excuses a rider who is not present; and on the rider's own statement she came down at 07:53, after the 07:51:40 cancellation and after the 07:50 expiry of the wait.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05058", "EV-GPS-05058"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-21", "POL-NS-22"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.free_wait.starts_from",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Nothing in the GPS evidence places the rider at the pickup at any time before the cancellation: the trace carries an empty rider_track, so her account that she came down at 07:53 is uncorroborated assertion, and the only fact it could support — a driver no-show under POL-NS-24 — fails on the arrival and contact record in any event.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-05058", "EV-TRIP-05058"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-24"],
      "relies_on": "gps_trace.rider_track",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Disclosure as POL-GEN-02 requires: EV-ADVIS-05058-01 is a MISSING artifact, impairs at weight 0.0, carries issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT and has no payload, so it carries no fact either way. Its absence does not open POL-GEN-26, because every fact the no-show rules need — when the driver arrived, that he waited past the free wait, and that he messaged and called before cancelling — is established on clean 1.0-weight artifacts, and the no-show test does not turn on traffic.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-05058-01", "EV-TRIP-05058", "EV-GPS-05058", "EV-CHAT-05058"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-02", "POL-GEN-26"],
      "relies_on": "evidence.EV-ADVIS-05058-01.admissibility.weight_multiplier",
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "This ruling stays with the AI. The contested amount is 5.00 SGD, below POL-GEN-22's 10.00 SGD band, and neither profile carries fraud_flags (both are 0), so no 0.95 confidence is required; under POL-NS-26 the AI ruling on a no-show is final, and no safety flag or indicator appears anywhere on this record to displace it under POL-GEN-21. The profile fields relied on here are only those POL-GEN-22 itself names.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-05058", "EV-DPROF-05058"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-22", "POL-NS-26", "POL-GEN-21"],
      "relies_on": "dispute.amount_contested_sgd",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "I do not claim the POL-NS-25 repeat no-show referral: the field that clause names, rider_profile.no_show_cancellations_30d, is not present on this snapshot, and POL-NS-25 applies only where the counter is present. The rider's no_show_disputes_30d and prior_no_show_flags are context only under POL-GEN-01 and ground nothing. That referral was never part of the money in any event; it would not have changed the 5.00 SGD payable to the driver.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-05058"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-25", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "relies_on": "rider_profile.no_show_cancellations_30d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Every artifact this side relies on is complete and unimpaired at weight 1.0 — the trip record, the driver-device trace, the chat log, the payments ledger and both profile snapshots — and no claim above rests on an artifact below 1.0 other than the MISSING advisory, which is disclosed as such. Under POL-GEN-25 each of these claims cites the evidence id it rests on and the clause it applies.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05058", "EV-GPS-05058", "EV-CHAT-05058", "EV-FARE-05058", "EV-DPROF-05058"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-25", "POL-GEN-02"],
      "relies_on": "evidence.admissibility.weight_multiplier",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "DRIVER_COMPENSATION",
    "amount_sgd": 5.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": 5.0,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "The 5.00 SGD no-show fee stands, and it is awarded to the driver. The state you are looking at — 5.00 SGD refunded to the rider and withheld from the driver at 07:59:40 on 24 Aug — was logged as an interim reversal after the rider's complaint, expressly 'pending review'. It is not a determination of this dispute, so the question is whether the no-show was properly taken, and the record says it was.\n\nFor the rider: the free wait under POL-NS-21 was served. The trip was scheduled for 07:45 and the driver arrived early, at 07:39:30, so the wait runs from the scheduled time (07:45) and expires at 07:50; the driver cancelled at 07:51:40, past it. The trip record's own derived free-wait figures apply exactly that measure (starts_from = scheduled_at, cancelled_after_free_wait = true, 400 s from the wait's start to the cancellation). Your point that the platform's on-screen timer started at the 07:39:35 arrival and expired at 07:44:35 is accurate as a fact about the app, but that timer did not produce this charge — the driver in fact waited until 07:51:40, past both the displayed timer and the clause's 07:50 deadline — so it is not a ground to void the fee. The arrival itself is corroborated by the GPS trace (nearest fix 1.76 m from the pickup, reported accuracy 3 m, inside the 50 m STANDARD radius; 47 fixes at 30 s intervals, 100% coverage, no gap over 30 s), as POL-NS-21 requires. On POL-GEN-26 you say nothing in the package proves you were absent; the facts the no-show rules need — when the driver arrived, that he waited out the free wait, and that he messaged and called before cancelling — are all established on unimpaired 1.0-weight artifacts, and your own account ('I came down at 7:53') places you at the pickup after the 07:51:40 cancellation and after the 07:50 expiry of the wait. Absence is therefore not an open question on this record, and there is no route to a human reviewer here.\n\nFor the driver: the arrival, the wait and the contact obligation are all made out. The driver sent two in-app messages (07:40:00, read 07:40:22; 07:46:20, read 07:46:30) and placed two in-app calls (07:47:30, unanswered, 28 s; 07:50:10, unanswered, 20 s), every one before the 07:51:40 cancellation, so POL-NS-23's obligation is met and no full refund arises on that ground — a point the rider's own case concedes. Under POL-NS-24 the driver-no-show deadline was 07:50 and he was at the pickup from 07:39:30, so there is no refund on that clause either, and no 5.00 SGD goodwill credit, which requires both a missed arrival deadline and a failure to attempt contact, and contact was attempted twice. With POL-NS-21, POL-NS-23 and POL-NS-24 all satisfied, POL-NS-22 makes the fee payable: it was charged at exactly the 5.00 SGD policy fee (fee_charged_sgd 5.00 against policy_fee_sgd 5.00, fee_matches_policy true), so POL-NS-22 directs DRIVER_COMPENSATION with the fee charged, 5.00 SGD, in both amount fields. Because the fee stands, POL-GEN-03's party-relative NO_ACTION does not apply: reading the outcome from your filing, the driver is owed the whole 5.00 SGD back.\n\nNo referral is produced. The fee charged equals the 5.00 SGD policy fee, so POL-NS-22's amount check adds nothing; POL-NS-24's goodwill credit does not fire (arrival on time, contact attempted); and POL-NS-25's repeat no-show referral cannot fire because the field that clause names, rider_profile.no_show_cancellations_30d, is not present on the snapshot, and the adjacent no-show fields are context only under POL-GEN-01.\n\nThe ruling rests on the trip record and the GPS trace, both admissibility weight 1.0 and mutually consistent, so the confidence cap is 1.0. The traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-05058-01, weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT) carries no fact and none is needed from it, since the no-show test does not turn on traffic. The contested amount is 5.00 SGD, below POL-GEN-22's 10.00 SGD band, neither profile carries fraud flags, and no safety indicator appears, so under POL-NS-26 this AI ruling is final."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
